WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:01.000
{Chapter 06}

00:18.830 --> 00:20.790
Why didn't you throw the same pitch?!

00:21.790 --> 00:22.790
I did.

00:22.791 --> 00:24.209
Don't lie to me!

00:24.210 --> 00:26.300
He couldn't hit a home run off that pitch!

00:33.390 --> 00:37.810
Did you hold back because
you didn't think I could catch it?!

00:39.810 --> 00:43.569
Why do I have to worry about your catching?

00:43.570 --> 00:45.440
Then how did he hit it?!

00:49.030 --> 00:51.029
That's pretty harsh.

00:51.030 --> 00:53.619
But I guess I feel the same way too.

00:53.620 --> 00:56.830
Was the fourth pitch a serious one?

00:59.250 --> 01:02.039
Kadowaki, please face
us in a exhibition game!

01:02.040 --> 01:04.089
Please give us another chance!

01:04.090 --> 01:07.260
Hey, Kadowaki,
would you consider an exhibition game?

01:07.920 --> 01:10.090
Could you request for one on your end?

01:10.760 --> 01:12.720
I'll strike you out next time.

01:13.720 --> 01:15.060
What did you say?

01:15.720 --> 01:17.389
Next time, I won't get hit off of.

01:17.390 --> 01:18.600
Not by anybody.

01:19.480 --> 01:24.230
Are you saying you're going to
pitch a perfect game against us?

01:24.690 --> 01:25.859
Yes.

01:25.860 --> 01:27.030
Please.

01:27.820 --> 01:30.779
Kaionji, what's with these guys?

01:30.780 --> 01:33.489
Are Nitta freshman all
little punks like them?

01:33.490 --> 01:36.490
No, these two are special.

01:39.450 --> 01:43.499
All right. I'm not sure what
I can do, but I'll give it a try.

01:43.500 --> 01:45.919
Really?! Thank you!

01:45.920 --> 01:47.920
I'll call you later for more details.

01:49.010 --> 01:52.430
I don't care what issues you may have.

02:12.110 --> 02:17.700
I've heard it said so many times

02:18.410 --> 02:24.580
How it's not going to work out

02:25.540 --> 02:31.090
That nothing will change

02:31.380 --> 02:37.600
Even if I pretended not to listen

02:38.050 --> 02:41.389
I knew it all

02:41.390 --> 02:44.559
I learned this from you

02:44.560 --> 02:52.560
That it's not a failure, even when it is

02:53.950 --> 03:00.539
When I thrust my feelings
on to the drifting clouds

03:00.540 --> 03:07.459
The quiet melodies push me forward

03:07.460 --> 03:13.969
Because the sky is so vast and free

03:13.970 --> 03:21.600
I decided that I wouldn't cry anymore

03:44.450 --> 03:45.370
Harada.

03:45.370 --> 03:46.330
Yes, sir?

03:46.331 --> 03:50.500
Why did you hold back on your
fourth pitch against Kadowaki?

03:51.630 --> 03:55.510
You thought Nagakura
couldn't catch it, didn't you?

03:55.970 --> 03:58.929
Were you afraid you might hurt him?

03:58.930 --> 04:02.219
Either way, I bet Nagakura is shocked.

04:02.220 --> 04:04.520
You betrayed him.

04:04.890 --> 04:07.639
Why couldn't you trust him?

04:07.640 --> 04:11.309
He would've done anything he
had to in order to stop that ball.

04:11.310 --> 04:14.650
And then he would've caught
the next one without a doubt.

04:15.070 --> 04:17.530
Did that belief in him
never cross your mind?

04:18.820 --> 04:21.119
You really are a kid.

04:21.120 --> 04:23.829
You don't know the basics of baseball.

04:23.830 --> 04:24.830
Kaionji.

04:25.410 --> 04:28.079
This one's gonna be real trouble.

04:28.080 --> 04:30.129
He doesn't understand anything.

04:30.130 --> 04:32.710
I didn't think he was this stupid.

04:38.930 --> 04:39.930
Yo.

04:39.930 --> 04:40.930
Hey.

04:43.010 --> 04:46.059
You couldn't do anything
against a junior high kid?

04:46.060 --> 04:47.179
No way.

04:47.180 --> 04:48.309
It's true.

04:48.310 --> 04:50.439
That's not something I'd joke about.

04:50.440 --> 04:52.519
So, now what?

04:52.520 --> 04:55.900
There's no way they'd let us have
an exhibition game against Nitta.

04:57.990 --> 04:59.199
You think?

04:59.200 --> 05:02.319
The school'd never sign off on it.

05:02.320 --> 05:04.279
What if we just played on our own?

05:04.280 --> 05:05.280
Huh?

05:05.740 --> 05:07.249
Leave the schools out of it.

05:07.250 --> 05:10.460
We'll just meet up and
play a game on our own.

05:10.830 --> 05:11.960
Shuugo...

05:13.750 --> 05:15.960
Are you being serious?

05:17.590 --> 05:18.799
Deadly serious.

05:18.800 --> 05:24.349
Yeah, but do you think we can really
just play a pickup game on our own?

05:24.350 --> 05:26.260
I guess it's never been done before.

05:29.390 --> 05:30.889
I'll take responsibility.

05:30.890 --> 05:32.149
Please, Shun.

05:32.150 --> 05:33.730
Back me up on this.

05:34.650 --> 05:39.280
I mean, it's not like it's cigarettes or
booze, so it shouldn't be a big deal.

05:40.030 --> 05:41.359
Shuugo.

05:41.360 --> 05:43.110
I bet that was your first time.

05:44.490 --> 05:51.079
Have you ever wanted to do something
so bad you'd go against the school?

05:51.080 --> 05:55.750
I bet you've never done something
this stupid before, have you?

05:56.710 --> 05:57.710
Shun.

05:59.710 --> 06:01.929
I'm Yokote's five-hole.

06:01.930 --> 06:06.509
I wanna meet the guy who's made
our Kadowaki Shuugo so goo-goo eyed.

06:06.510 --> 06:10.269
He's the first person who's
ever drawn you out like this.

06:10.270 --> 06:12.019
How could I not be interested?

06:12.020 --> 06:15.059
I'm getting all excited here
'cause I want a go at him too.

06:15.060 --> 06:19.030
It sounds dirty when you say it.

06:19.440 --> 06:21.779
I bet he's a real looker.

06:21.780 --> 06:25.199
You can meet him in
the batter's box yourself.

06:25.200 --> 06:27.200
It'll be your first time
experiencing that too.

06:32.290 --> 06:33.290
Seiha.

06:37.500 --> 06:41.050
I'm not going to sleep in your
room with you anymore, got it?

06:41.380 --> 06:42.469
I know.

06:42.470 --> 06:44.469
My fever's already down.

06:44.470 --> 06:47.050
Then hurry up and go back to your own room.

06:49.680 --> 06:52.310
Did you have a fight with Gou?

06:53.980 --> 06:55.810
Why do you ask that?

06:56.940 --> 06:58.149
Because I can tell.

06:58.150 --> 07:02.110
You seemed hurt the last
time you had a fight with Gou.

07:05.070 --> 07:07.119
It'll be okay.

07:07.120 --> 07:08.320
What will?

07:08.660 --> 07:11.909
Gou told me something before.

07:11.910 --> 07:16.289
He said, "Your brother
won't lose to anybody."

07:16.290 --> 07:20.380
I think Gou really likes you.

07:22.210 --> 07:26.720
So I'm sure if you say
you're sorry, he'll forgive you.

07:30.680 --> 07:32.470
There's a phone call for you, Takumi.

07:34.100 --> 07:35.519
Is it Gou?

07:35.520 --> 07:36.639
No.

07:36.640 --> 07:39.270
It sounded like a cute girl.

07:43.570 --> 07:44.819
Hello?

07:44.820 --> 07:46.450
<i>Harada, it's me.</i>

07:47.530 --> 07:50.329
<i>I just got a call from Kadowaki.</i>

07:50.330 --> 07:53.409
<i>He said to be ready because
there's definitely going to be a game.</i>

07:53.410 --> 07:56.829
<i>Seems like there's a good
chance it's going to happen.</i>

07:56.830 --> 07:58.879
<i>I just wanted to let you know.</i>

07:58.880 --> 07:59.920
<i>That's all.</i>

08:01.170 --> 08:02.209
Captain.

08:02.210 --> 08:03.210
<i>Hm?</i>

08:04.130 --> 08:06.839
Um, have you called Gou too?

08:06.840 --> 08:09.930
<i>Yeah, I just called him.</i>

08:10.600 --> 08:12.099
Did he say anything?

08:12.100 --> 08:13.429
<i>No.</i>

08:13.430 --> 08:17.560
<i>But he sounded really
excited about playing this game.</i>

08:18.560 --> 08:20.439
<i>Oh, Harada.</i>

08:20.440 --> 08:21.689
Yes?

08:21.690 --> 08:25.989
<i>Don't really dwell on what the coach said.</i>

08:25.990 --> 08:30.239
<i>A worried battery isn't much use.</i>

08:30.240 --> 08:32.659
<i>Honestly? They only get in the way.</i>

08:32.660 --> 08:33.700
<i>Well, talk to you later.</i>

08:36.410 --> 08:38.540
I'll go put the phone back for you.

09:14.530 --> 09:15.530
Takumi?

09:15.950 --> 09:17.080
Get down here, Gou.

09:22.500 --> 09:23.500
Gou!

09:23.501 --> 09:25.590
Where are you going at this hour?

09:27.170 --> 09:28.170
Oh.

09:28.171 --> 09:30.010
Are you going somewhere with Takumi?

09:32.720 --> 09:35.010
Gou, your mom's talking to you.

10:00.750 --> 10:03.040
You idiot! You're just...

10:06.040 --> 10:08.670
Dammit, you humiliated me.

10:12.340 --> 10:14.050
Why aren't you fighting back?!

10:14.390 --> 10:15.889
You're way bigger than me!

10:15.890 --> 10:18.059
You think I could ever
beat you in a real fight?!

10:18.060 --> 10:19.349
Coward!

10:19.350 --> 10:22.310
You can't talk big unless
you're gripping a ball, is that it?!

10:23.140 --> 10:24.729
I've had enough of your bullshit!

10:24.730 --> 10:25.650
Stop screwing around!

10:25.651 --> 10:27.020
I'm not screwing around!

10:27.440 --> 10:30.649
I've never screwed around
when it comes to you!

10:30.650 --> 10:32.899
What am I to you?!

10:32.900 --> 10:35.410
Some catcher you can't
pitch to without holding back?!

10:36.030 --> 10:37.030
Dammit.

10:37.700 --> 10:41.329
How did you look at me when
you threw that fourth pitch?

10:41.330 --> 10:44.420
What kind of catcher
is pitied by his pitcher?!

10:44.830 --> 10:49.209
The real person I should be
fighting isn't Yokote or the principal!

10:49.210 --> 10:50.420
It's you!

10:51.130 --> 10:52.669
Just you watch.

10:52.670 --> 10:54.430
I'm not going to lose to you.

10:55.340 --> 10:57.010
I'm never letting you pity me.

10:58.260 --> 11:02.140
I'm going to make you see
that I'm the best catcher for you.

11:02.930 --> 11:05.310
You're going to be sorry.

11:06.480 --> 11:07.810
Just remember that, Takumi.

11:11.030 --> 11:12.110
I will.

11:48.100 --> 11:50.189
Look, Higashidani.

11:50.190 --> 11:52.609
Look what happened to our great Harada.

11:52.610 --> 11:55.819
His poor face is ruined.

11:55.820 --> 11:59.199
It's a shame. I mean, it'd be
one thing if it were just your face.

11:59.200 --> 12:01.699
Wait, what's that supposed to mean?

12:01.700 --> 12:04.789
I'm just as good looking as Harada.

12:04.790 --> 12:08.210
I'm at least in the top five
hottest guys at Nitta East.

12:08.580 --> 12:10.959
Who the hell would
rank you in the top five?

12:10.960 --> 12:12.709
Will you two shut up already?

12:12.710 --> 12:14.919
Who did this to you?

12:14.920 --> 12:16.299
Was it Otomurai?

12:16.300 --> 12:17.469
An elephant.

12:17.470 --> 12:18.470
Elephant?

12:18.550 --> 12:20.139
We keep an elephant.

12:20.140 --> 12:21.970
And he had a little fit.

12:22.760 --> 12:24.389
An elephant, you say?

12:24.390 --> 12:26.730
One the great Harada keeps at home?

12:32.020 --> 12:33.110
Kadowaki.

12:33.820 --> 12:37.110
So that's Kadowaki from Yokote?

12:45.080 --> 12:48.000
How does the last Sunday of
the month sound to you, Kaionji?

12:48.870 --> 12:49.959
Huh?

12:49.960 --> 12:51.000
For our game.

12:52.040 --> 12:54.249
You're going to request a game for us?

12:54.250 --> 12:57.919
I was told we couldn't
go through the school.

12:57.920 --> 12:58.920
But we'll still do it.

12:59.760 --> 13:00.760
Harada.

13:01.390 --> 13:03.549
I made sure to tell them.

13:03.550 --> 13:07.390
How there's a first year who said
he'd pitch a perfect game against us.

13:09.390 --> 13:11.059
They all want a shot at you.

13:11.060 --> 13:12.269
That's why we're doing this.

13:12.270 --> 13:14.399
Our schools have nothing to do with this.

13:14.400 --> 13:15.900
What do you mean?

13:16.230 --> 13:20.239
Come Sunday, if it's just a bunch of
kids getting together to play baseball,

13:20.240 --> 13:22.910
we don't need any pesky permission.

13:23.990 --> 13:25.910
Oh, I didn't think of that!

13:26.870 --> 13:29.209
I've come here to get your okay.

13:29.210 --> 13:31.290
So? You in?

13:31.580 --> 13:32.789
Of course!

13:32.790 --> 13:34.499
I owe you, Kadowaki!

13:34.500 --> 13:37.800
Hey, you'll be sorry if
you keep talking like that.

13:38.880 --> 13:39.880
Harada.

13:40.130 --> 13:41.130
Yes.

13:41.680 --> 13:45.509
I hope you're ready to back up your words.

13:45.510 --> 13:47.639
I won't accept any crappy pitching.

13:47.640 --> 13:49.680
You'd better not let us down.

13:50.140 --> 13:51.190
Of course.

13:51.810 --> 13:55.690
Don't come crying to us if
we crush your big future star.

13:57.570 --> 13:58.939
Hey, don't get cocky.

13:58.940 --> 14:01.399
And don't go crying to your
mom when we beat you.

14:01.400 --> 14:03.200
It'll affect your exams.

14:04.740 --> 14:06.989
We'll play where we met yesterday.

14:06.990 --> 14:08.539
You come to us.

14:08.540 --> 14:11.709
In exchange, we'll arrange
for the umps and everything.

14:11.710 --> 14:12.960
Copy that.

14:15.330 --> 14:17.959
Sorry to have interrupted your practice.

14:17.960 --> 14:20.970
Hey, Kadowaki. How'd you get here, anyway?

14:21.470 --> 14:22.679
I ran.

14:22.680 --> 14:24.470
It was just the right distance.

14:31.480 --> 14:34.689
He ran all the way here from Yokote?

14:34.690 --> 14:35.690
Yeah.

14:40.280 --> 14:44.609
Coach. Could we start scrimmaging
tomorrow to prepare for our game?

14:44.610 --> 14:45.699
You do that.

14:45.700 --> 14:46.989
I'll leave it to you.

14:46.990 --> 14:47.620
Yes, sir.

14:47.910 --> 14:50.079
The problem is our battery.

14:50.080 --> 14:51.370
What do you want to do?

14:51.790 --> 14:53.499
Harada, Nagakura.

14:53.500 --> 14:55.120
You're on the white team.

14:55.420 --> 14:58.589
You'll get to face us regulars,
and we won't go easy on you.

14:58.590 --> 14:59.590
Right.

15:03.880 --> 15:05.885
Yokote Baseball Park

15:05.886 --> 15:07.890
Yokote Baseball Park

15:25.400 --> 15:27.740
Hey. You watching your girlfriend?

15:28.410 --> 15:30.660
Yokote Second

15:30.661 --> 15:32.910
Nitta East

15:40.840 --> 15:42.759
Is that him?

15:42.760 --> 15:43.920
Yeah.

15:44.800 --> 15:46.219
I see.

15:46.220 --> 15:48.429
That's quite the princess.

15:48.430 --> 15:49.799
What?

15:49.800 --> 15:54.599
I was wondering who this guy Kadowaki was
raving over was, and he's just some skinny kid.

15:54.600 --> 15:57.979
Everyone's a skinny kid compared to you.

15:57.980 --> 15:58.940
What's that?

15:58.941 --> 16:02.689
Go do some practice swings in
front of the dugout to scare that pitcher.

16:02.690 --> 16:05.109
Is that really necessary?

16:05.110 --> 16:06.450
Just do it.

16:15.370 --> 16:17.459
He's leveling the mound.

16:17.460 --> 16:21.710
That freshman doesn't seem to be
fazed that he's pitching against Yokote.

16:23.000 --> 16:25.209
So he's not even nervous?

16:25.210 --> 16:27.720
That's some balls.

16:34.720 --> 16:37.729
Let's crush him, then,
before it's too late.

16:37.730 --> 16:39.730
I'm talking about your girlfriend.

16:40.440 --> 16:44.730
He's pretty, but he's got a bad attitude.

16:47.240 --> 16:48.529
You really think we can crush him?

16:48.530 --> 16:50.240
Easily.

16:50.950 --> 16:52.490
Jouno. Hagi.

16:54.370 --> 16:56.499
Study that pitcher hard.

16:56.500 --> 16:58.829
He's going to be an
issue for us before long.

16:58.830 --> 16:59.830
Right!

17:03.290 --> 17:05.000
Play ball!

17:36.990 --> 17:39.040
Strike three! Change sides!

17:43.830 --> 17:44.710
Hagi.

17:44.710 --> 17:45.710
Yes?

17:46.920 --> 17:50.800
The only batter we need to worry
about is their cleanup, Kaionji.

17:51.260 --> 17:53.759
They're mostly a defensive team.

17:53.760 --> 17:55.800
Just stay loose.

18:10.360 --> 18:11.360
Ball four.

18:27.750 --> 18:28.840
Change sides.

18:30.760 --> 18:32.260
Yokote Second

18:32.261 --> 18:33.760
Nitta East

18:41.140 --> 18:43.559
It's your date with your beloved princess.

18:43.560 --> 18:45.440
Go have fun.

18:52.360 --> 18:54.699
Good to see you again, Nagakura.

18:54.700 --> 18:55.450
Likewise.

18:55.451 --> 18:57.529
That pitch is coming, right?

18:57.530 --> 18:58.530
Of course.

18:59.280 --> 19:00.450
Can you catch it?

19:00.910 --> 19:01.910
I will.

19:03.120 --> 19:04.120
Play.

19:09.630 --> 19:10.920
Strike one!

19:21.100 --> 19:23.390
Strike three! You're out!

19:30.770 --> 19:34.610
Well, even you can get struck
out by a lucky fluke once in a while.

19:35.530 --> 19:37.610
That wasn't a fluke.

19:42.870 --> 19:45.080
You guys need to get it together.

19:46.920 --> 19:48.880
Hey, just let him throw it.

19:49.590 --> 19:52.379
Give me the same pitch
he threw to Kadowaki.

19:52.380 --> 19:54.050
Or was that just a fluke?

19:55.470 --> 19:57.589
He needs a new catcher, though.

19:57.590 --> 19:58.590
What?

19:58.840 --> 20:02.350
Could you catch the ball
if he pitches even faster?

20:03.640 --> 20:05.139
No, right?

20:05.140 --> 20:06.849
What are you saying?

20:06.850 --> 20:09.730
Look how troubled your princess is.

20:10.610 --> 20:13.860
You're not giving him any
signs, and you're not in position.

20:14.320 --> 20:16.029
The poor thing.

20:16.030 --> 20:19.240
He's so lost, he doesn't know what to do.

20:21.830 --> 20:24.199
Batter, no talking in the box.

20:24.200 --> 20:25.870
I apologize, sir!

20:30.540 --> 20:31.540
Play on.

20:33.920 --> 20:34.920
Gou.

20:51.770 --> 20:52.770
<i>That's getting through.</i>

21:21.800 --> 21:24.180
Summer's peak came and went

21:26.560 --> 21:32.859
That's what the weather report said

21:32.860 --> 21:39.365
But it still feels like
the city is restless

21:47.200 --> 21:55.200
The evening bells of 5 p.m.
resonate inside my heart today

22:02.130 --> 22:08.535
Clouding me with something
convenient like "destiny"

22:20.511 --> 22:24.199
It's the final fireworks of the year

22:24.200 --> 22:27.910
I will remember them for years to come

22:27.911 --> 22:31.619
I will remember them for years to come

22:31.620 --> 22:33.475
Are you here? You're probably not

22:33.476 --> 22:35.329
Are you here? You're probably not

22:35.330 --> 22:37.210
I'm sure you're not

22:37.211 --> 22:39.089
I'm sure you're not

22:39.090 --> 22:40.905
Will I be able to say it if I see you?

22:40.906 --> 22:42.719
Will I be able to say it if I see you?

22:42.720 --> 22:45.535
I close my eyes and dream

22:45.536 --> 22:48.350
I close my eyes and dream

22:58.090 --> 23:00.679
<i>Gou, I brought you some potatoes!</i>

23:00.680 --> 23:01.680
<i>Potatoes?</i>

23:05.470 --> 23:07.849
<i>Let's play!</i>

23:07.850 --> 23:09.389
<i>Play?</i>

23:09.390 --> 23:10.729
<i>Play what?</i>

23:10.730 --> 23:11.730
<i>Baseball!</i>

23:15.730 --> 23:17.940
<i>I've got some big news today.</i>

23:18.900 --> 23:21.109
<i>Then please keep it short.</i>

23:21.110 --> 23:23.595
Episode 8: "The Autumn of Endings"
